          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "l'orchestre comes from Latin orchēstra, a borrowing from Greek orkhḗstra \"the space where the chorus danced\" (EtymDB), built on orkheîsthai \"to dance\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
